stxlib::glyphs, the font reader and the hinter

The font reader of stxlib::glyphs (include/stxlib/font_file.hpp and
src/algorithms/glyphs/font_file.cpp, font_truetype.cpp, font_cff.cpp,
font_reader.hpp) and its hinter (include/stxlib/glyph_hinter.hpp and
src/algorithms/glyphs/hinter.hpp, hinter.cpp, hinter_outline.cpp,
hinter_segments.cpp, hinter_edges.cpp, hinter_metrics.cpp, hinter_fit.cpp,
hinter_align.cpp, hinter_tables.inc) are part of STXlib and are STXlib's own
code, under STXlib's licence (the repository's LICENSE). They are a
conversion to house-style C++ of the design of two projects, each offered
under the MIT licence or the Apache License 2.0; it is taken under the MIT
licence, and carries their notices, which follow unchanged.

- ttf-parser 0.25.1 (https://github.com/harfbuzz/ttf-parser), by Yevhenii
  Reizner: the table directory and collections, the face's numbers, the
  character maps, advances, a glyph's range in glyf and the two passes over
  a simple glyph's flags and coordinates, the indexes and dictionaries of
  CFF and the operators of its charstrings.
- Skrifa 0.50.0 and read-fonts 0.47.0 (https://github.com/googlefonts/
  fontations), by the Fontations developers: a composite glyph put together
  in whole numbers, the outline placed by its left side bearing, a scaled
  glyph's parts scaled on their own, and a CFF glyph's coordinates in whole
  font units with the lines and points that are left out; and the whole of
  the hinter: Skrifa's auto-hinter (src/outline/autohint), with its table of
  scripts, styles, blue zone characters and character ranges
  (generated/generated_autohint_styles.rs), from which hinter_tables.inc is
  made by tools/gen_hinter_tables.py.

Skrifa's auto-hinter follows the auto-hinter of the FreeType Project (the
autofit module, by David Turner, Robert Wilhelm and Werner Lemberg) place
by place, as its source says at each, and its table is made from that
module's. STXlib's hinter was converted from Skrifa's and not from
FreeType's source; it owes its method to both. Portions of this software are copyright (c) The
FreeType Project (https://freetype.org). All rights reserved.

The rasterizer of stxlib::glyphs (glyph_mask.hpp, mask.cpp, chords.hpp,
flatten.hpp, centres.hpp, reciprocal.hpp) is not a conversion of any of
these.

